5417] [17592186436342 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "81fb17ab-9d92-5133-9b83-605ee50e698b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\in V.$ Given that $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent and $-{v}_{3}=2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2},$ which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0$ has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$\n\nIII. $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is a linearly dependent set" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8366d224-f20d-5615-aa2b-700c64d6cb9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436343 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, solving the equation $-{v}_{3}=2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}$ for ${v}_{1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\frac{3}{2}{v}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}_{3}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-{v}_{3}=2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2},$ we have that\n\n$$\n2{v}_{1}-3{v}_{2}+1\\cdot {v}_{3}=0.\n$$\n\nAs a result, ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0$ has a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0$ has a non-zero solution, the set $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436344 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436344 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "98ee88b4-255d-5371-b8e0-162d265834c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436344 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125158 #edb/ref 1759218